<title>NEW ZEALAND: Wang half-yr profit rises to NZ$1.72 mln.</title>
<headline>Wang half-yr profit rises to NZ$1.72 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr to December 31.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    1.72 vs 1.56</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			  19.88 vs 18.31</p>
<p>    Turnover			     33.93 vs 38.06</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			 2.60 vs 2.36</p>
<p>    Tax				     0.87 vs 0.80</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)   17.34 vs same</p>
<p>Note - Wang New Zealand Ltd is a computer and software supplier.</p>
<p>Blue Star, a unit of U.S. Office Products had increased its shareholding in Wang NZ to 88.6 percent, Wang NZ said. Wang Laboratories Inc had maintained a shareholding of 9.8 percent leaving other minority interests with 1.6 percent of the company's stock.</p>
<p>Blue Star has an option to acquire the balance of Wang Laboratories shares. Wang NZ said when Blue Star had passed the 90 percent threshold allowing compulsory acquisition of the remaining stock, Wang NZ would de-list from the Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>&quot;As we go into the second half, the indicators are all extremely positive,&quot; Wang NZ said.</p>
<p>&quot;Our internal morale has never been higher and we are well placed to continue to exceed our plan forecasts.&quot;</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
